.TH FL-DISPLAYS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.8" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-displays \- screen arrangement
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-displays\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the screens and sets the resolution and refresh rate, the scale, the
rotation and the position of each one, or turns a screen off. The same editor
is the Displays page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1).
.PP
\fBApply\fR changes the screens at once and asks whether to keep the new
arrangement; without an answer it goes back to the old one after 15 seconds.
At least one screen stays on.
.PP
fl-displays uses the wlr-output-management protocol, so it also works on
other wlroots compositors such as sway, labwc and Hyprland. Under
\fBfl-wm\fR(1) a kept arrangement is written to the \fB[output:\fIname\fB]\fR
sections of \fI~/.config/fldesktop/wm.ini\fR; on other compositors it lasts
until the compositor restarts.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-settings\fR(1), \fBfl-wm\fR(1)
